<title>UK: UK unhappy with two firms on pensions mis-selling.</title>
<headline>UK unhappy with two firms on pensions mis-selling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Junior Treasury Minister Helen Liddell said on Tuesday she was dissatisfied with the response of two insurance companies -- the Sedgwick Group Plc and Legal and General Group Plc -- to her appeal for speedier compensation for mis-selling of personal pensions.</p>
<p>Liddell spoke last month to representatives of 24 firms asking them to perform to better standards, and said in a parliamentary written answer she had received satisfactory policy statements in response from most of the firms concerned.</p>
</text>
